{
  "title": "Smooth particle mesh Ewald / SPME",
  "html": "<h1>Smooth particle mesh Ewald / SPME</h1><p>SPME approximates Ewald structure factors using smooth cardinal B-splines. Treat it as a specific interpolation-and-force construction rather than a synonym for every PME implementation.</p><h2 id=\"model\">Problem and representative equations</h2><p>Let uᵢ be particle coordinates in mesh units and Mₚ a cardinal B-spline of order p, not degree p. The product below is the local tensor assignment in three dimensions. Fourier structure factors require a correction for the spline response.</p><div class=\"math-block\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><munder><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></munder><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"/><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1.</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q_{m_xm_ym_z}=\\sum_iq_i\\prod_{d\\in\\{x,y,z\\}}M_p(u_{id}-m_d),\\qquad \\deg M_p=p-1.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0307em;vertical-align:-0.3473em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">Q</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">m</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1645em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.357em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.0714em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.5em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">x</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.143em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">m</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1645em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.357em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.0714em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.5em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2819em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">m</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1645em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.357em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.0714em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.5em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.143em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3473em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.566em;vertical-align:-1.516em;\"></span><span class=\"mop op-limits\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.05em;\"><span style=\"top:-1.8723em;margin-left:0em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mop op-symbol large-op\">∑</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.2777em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop op-limits\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.05em;\"><span style=\"top:-1.809em;margin-left:0em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">d</span><span class=\"mrel mtight\">∈</span><span class=\"mopen mtight\">{</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">x</span><span class=\"mpunct mtight\">,</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"mpunct mtight\">,</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span><span class=\"mclose mtight\">}</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mop op-symbol large-op\">∏</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.516em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.109em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">u</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">d</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0361em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">d</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">de<span style=\"margin-right:0.0139em;\">g</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.109em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.</span></span></span></span></span></div><h2 id=\"algorithm\">Algorithm</h2><p>Spread charge over p neighboring mesh points in each direction, evaluate a corrected reciprocal mesh energy by FFT, and obtain forces using derivatives of the assignment in analytical differentiation. Record the spline order and mesh together with whether differentiation is analytical or in Fourier space.</p><h2 id=\"conditions\">Conditions and pitfalls</h2><p>Smooth assignment alone does not guarantee both energy consistency and exact net-force cancellation. Ewald neutrality, boundary and self-term conventions still apply. Comparisons with original PME should control error tolerance and differentiation rules, not merely the number of mesh points.</p><p>The companion also uses analytical energy gradients with B-spline orders 4/6. Discrete energy–force consistency, common-translation mesh effects and net force are separate observables. Finite-mesh aliasing generally permits nonzero net force; exact momentum conservation is not claimed.</p><h2 id=\"verification\">What to check</h2><p>Measure force errors against the same converged Ewald reference and check energy finite differences. Report common-translation mesh effects and total force separately. Ensure real-space truncation is not hiding the reciprocal-space convergence trend.</p><p>The design compares 16³/24³/40³ meshes and several common translations against matching direct-Ewald and independent theta references. It separates partition of unity/charge, energy differences, RMS/maximum force errors and real-space truncation; it supplies no evidence for long MD or original PME.</p><h2 id=\"scoped-examples\">Check fixed inputs: separate scoped releases</h2><p>Check each example’s inputs, observables, diagnostic definitions and scope. What a passing check establishes depends on its acceptance criteria and differs from a general mathematical guarantee. Historical inputs, measurements and criteria are preserved.</p><article class=\"resource-summary\" id=\"supplement-spme\"><h3>Mesh/order convergence of B-spline smooth PME</h3><p>Computation for a fixed target</p><p>A small smooth-PME example assigns charge with B-splines and evaluates the Ewald reciprocal contribution by FFT.</p><p>Finite-mesh aliasing permits nonzero net force for this energy-gradient variant; that diagnostic is reported. No exact momentum conservation, long MD, original PME, optimized P³M or slab validation is claimed.</p><p><a href=\"/numerical-methods-atlas/validation/spme/?lang=en\">Input, results and acceptance</a> · <a href=\"/numerical-methods-atlas/en/read/validation-particles/#spme\">Method, equations and sources</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particles/run.py\">Code: run.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particles/electrostatics.py\">Code: electrostatics.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particles/fmm.py\">Code: fmm.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particles/transport.py\">Code: transport.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particles/test_particles.py\">Tests: test_particles.py</a> · <a href=\"/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particles/atlas-particles-2026-11-22.zip\">Release ZIP</a> · <a href=\"/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particles/results/result.json\">Saved results</a> · <a href=\"/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particles/verification.json\">Independent-extraction rerun receipt</a></p></article><article class=\"resource-summary\" id=\"supplement-spme-convergence\"><h3>SPME: mesh, interpolation order, mesh phase and conservation</h3><p>Computation for a fixed target</p><p>Compare B-spline SPME with the same independent theta reference; measure mesh/order/phase effects, charge partition, energy gradients and net force.</p><p>Finite-mesh aliasing generally gives nonzero net force for this energy-gradient variant. No exact momentum conservation, arbitrary-configuration error bound, long MD, original PME or every SPME variant is certified.</p><p><a href=\"/numerical-methods-atlas/validation/spme-convergence/?lang=en\">Input, results and acceptance</a> · <a href=\"/numerical-methods-atlas/en/read/validation-particle-transport/#spme-convergence\">Method, equations and sources</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/run.py\">Code: run.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/longrange_experiments.py\">Code: longrange_experiments.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/electrostatics.py\">Code: electrostatics.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/fmm.py\">Code: fmm.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/kinetic_experiments.py\">Code: kinetic_experiments.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/kinetics.py\">Code: kinetics.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/test_kinetics.py\">Tests: test_kinetics.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/test_longrange.py\">Tests: test_longrange.py</a> · <a href=\"https://hrkoyama.github.io/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/test_runner.py\">Tests: test_runner.py</a> · <a href=\"/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/atlas-particle-transport-2026-11-22.zip\">Release ZIP</a> · <a href=\"/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/results/result.json\">Saved results</a> · <a href=\"/code/validated-examples/2026-11-22/particle-transport/verification.json\">Independent-extraction rerun receipt</a></p></article><h2 id=\"publication-scope\">Publication scope and related entries</h2><p>The historical reading, equations, sources and release are preserved; a separate companion release supplies bounded checks for fixed conditions. This does not mean every general verification suggestion above has been executed. Consult each release’s dedicated page and saved record for inputs, references, checks and limits.</p><ul><li><a href=\"/numerical-methods-atlas/methods/spme/?lang=en\">Smooth particle mesh Ewald / SPME</a></li></ul><h2 id=\"sources\">Primary publications, supporting sources and review scope</h2><p>Distinguish original research, later variants, author monographs, pedagogical articles and official references. Bibliographic verification differs from consulting selected passages; neither implies a full-paper audit or numerical reproduction. Access-depth notes accompany each source.</p><ol class=\"reading-sources\"><li id=\"source-essmann1995spme\"><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1063/1.470117\">Essmann, Ulrich and Perera, Lalith and Berkowitz, Max L. and Darden, Tom and Lee, Hsing and Pedersen, Lee G. (1995). A smooth particle mesh Ewald method</a>. The Journal of Chemical Physics<p>Research publication: proposal or related formulation · Bibliography checked · <a href=\"https://biomolmd.org/mw/images/e/e0/Spme.pdf\">Consulted record</a></p><p>Reviewed as a source for priority-method metadata. The individual method records distinguish reference roles, relevant full-text passages, abstracts and bibliographic checks; this does not imply a new numerical validation.</p></li><li id=\"source-darden1993pme\"><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1063/1.464397\">Darden, Tom and York, Darrin and Pedersen, Lee (1993). Particle mesh Ewald: An N log(N) method for Ewald sums in large systems</a>. The Journal of Chemical Physics<p>Research publication: proposal or related formulation · Bibliography checked · <a href=\"https://theory.rutgers.edu/resources/pdfs/1.464397.pdf\">Consulted record</a></p><p>Reviewed as a source for priority-method metadata. The individual method records distinguish reference roles, relevant full-text passages, abstracts and bibliographic checks; this does not imply a new numerical validation.</p></li></ol>",
